## Execution Readiness Checklist

- [ ] Atomic tasks: one clear action per checkbox.
- [ ] Exact paths: every task names precise repo-relative or fully qualified paths.
- [ ] Explicit commands: every task provides verbatim execution and verification commands.
- [ ] Clear ordering: prerequisites and strict task order are explicit.
- [ ] Verification per step: every task has exactly one authoritative acceptance check.
- [ ] No assumed context: an unfamiliar agent can execute without extra repository exploration.
- [ ] Concrete examples: format-sensitive tasks include templates, snippets, or exact expected output.
- [ ] Error recovery: every task defines a safe fallback for common failures.

